"A":"All members must do it.","B":"Members have the option of doing it.","C":"The organiser is responsible."},"items":[{"q":11,"text":"Taking tents"},{"q":12,"text":"Booking campsites"},{"q":13,"text":"Taking bicycles"},{"q":14,"text":"Buying train tickets"},{"q":15,"text":"Buying tickets for a football match"},{"q":16,"text":"Collecting information about the area of the tour"}]},{"kind":"matching","range":"Questions 17–20","instruction":"Which location has the following attraction?","word_limit":"Choose FOUR letters, A–H. Use each letter once.","title":"Tour locations and attractions","choices":{"A":"farming museum","B":"horseriding","C":"locally produced food","D":"market selling clothes","E":"old ruins","F":"steam railway","G":"transport museum","H":"water sports"},"items":[{"q":17,"text":"Westbury"},{"q":18,"text":"Cluny"},{"q":19,"text":"Pennerley"},{"q":20,"text":"Farlow"}]}]},{"number":3,"label":"SECTION 3","range":"Questions 21–30","blocks":[{"kind":"notes","range":"Questions 21–22","instruction":"Complete the notes below.","word_limit":"Write ONE WORD ONLY for each answer.","title":"Book report feedback","items":[["Hand in book reports with next assignment."],["Check accuracy of the ",{"q":21}," in the last section."],["Try to give more ",{"q":22},"."],["Need to expand ideas to improve grade."]]},{"kind":"notes","range":"Questions 23–27","instruction":"Answer the questions below.","word_limit":"Write the answer in the space provided.","title":"Karen’s presentation","items":[["When will Karen give her presentation? ",{"q":23}],["What must she do during the presentation? ",{"q":24}],["By which date must she submit an abstract? ",{"q":25}],["Where will the presentation take place? ",{"q":26}],["Who will grade her presentation? ",{"q":27}]]},{"kind":"choose_many","range":"Questions 28–30","instruction":"Choose THREE correct answers.","question":"Which THREE modules will Karen study next year?","questions":[28,29,30],"max_selections":3,"options":{"A":"Communication Skills","B":"Data Collection","C":"Discourse Analysis","D":"Language and Society","E":"Phonology","F":"Psycholinguistics","G":"Research Methodology","H":"Social Interaction"}}]},{"number":4,"label":"SECTION 4","range":"Questions 31–40","blocks":[{"kind":"notes_groups","range":"Questions 31–40","instruction":"Complete the notes below.","word_limit":"Write ONE WORD ONLY for each answer.","title":"Extinction of Species","groups":[{"heading":"Recent problems in Australia","items":[["A species of parrot is under threat due to the production of wind energy."],["Several species of ",{"q":31}," are at risk because of increased housing."],["Loss of food source due to pesticides is affecting many animals, especially ",{"q":32},"."],["Production of single crops like ",{"q":33}," is harming wildlife."]]},{"heading":"Attitude to endangered animals","items":[["Can be influenced by the ",{"q":34}," (e.g. the panda)."],["People are less concerned about smaller animals, e.g. ",{"q":35},"."],["Some animals are ignored because they are viewed with ",{"q":36},";"],["as our ",{"q":37}," in terms of food;"],["with disgust."]]},{"heading":"Reasons for preventing extinction","items":[["to improve our knowledge of the ecosystem."],["The ecosystem needs to be ",{"q":38}," to be stable."],["Some types of ",{"q":39}," can help to signal environmental problems."],["Animals can help in medicine, e.g. improved well-being for people from having a pet."],["Cobwebs help with medical disorders related to ",{"q":40},"."]]}]}]}],"answer_key":{"1":["C"],"2":["E"],"3":["F"],"4":["8","eight"],"5":["clean"],"6":["signs"],"7":["C"],"8":["B"],"9":["A"],"10":["C"],"11":["A"],"12":["C"],"13":["A"],"14":["C"],"15":["B"],"16":["C"],"17":["E"],"18":["A"],"19":["C"],"20":["G"],"21":["references"],"22":["examples"],"23":["at the next seminar","the next seminar","next seminar"],"24":["explain the experiment","explain experiment"],"25":["26 November","26th November","26th of November","November 26","November 26th